language ESSENCE' 1.0
$ csplib_006_golomb_rulers: an Essence' model from DCP Rosetta.
$
$ A Golomb ruler is a set of m integers 0 = a_1 < a_2 < ... < a_m such that the m(m-1)/2 differences a_j - a_i, for 1 <= i < j <= m, are all distinct. Such a ruler has m marks and length a_m. Find an optimal ruler, one of minimum length.
$
$ Save this file as model.eprime. Download `csplib_006_golomb_rulers.json` and `dcp_convert_essence.py` from the
$ problem's page:
$   https://dcp-bench.github.io/DCP-Rosetta/problems/csplib_006_golomb_rulers.html
$ Convert the instances once, then run the first one with Savile Row 1.11 (it needs Java); the
$ solution is written to `csplib_006_golomb_rulers_1.param.solution`:
$   python dcp_convert_essence.py csplib_006_golomb_rulers.json
$   savilerow model.eprime csplib_006_golomb_rulers_1.param -run-solver

$ size: the number of marks m of the ruler
given size : int(2..)

$ marks[p]: the position of mark p (indices 1-based, so the first mark a_1 = 0 is marks[1]); size*size is a safe upper bound on the length of an optimal ruler, chosen only to give the domain a finite range
find marks : matrix indexed by [int(1..size)] of int(0..size*size)
$ length: the length of the ruler, the position of its last mark
find length : int(0..size*size)

minimising length
such that
$ the first mark is at position 0
marks[1] = 0,
$ the marks are in increasing order
forAll p : int(1..size-1) . marks[p] < marks[p+1],
$ the last mark gives the length of the ruler
length = marks[size],
$ the differences marks[j] - marks[i] over all pairs i < j are all distinct
allDiff([marks[j] - marks[i] | i : int(1..size), j : int(i+1..size)])
